Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::stamping_reserves_six_bits_and_keeps_the_other_hundred_and_twenty_two`.

The defect: `v4_from_random` clears one bit too many in the variant byte (`0x1f` for `0x3f`). The printed form
still says variant `10`, so every sample looks right, and the stamp quietly discards a bit of the
caller's entropy.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(stamped[8] & 0x3f, raw[8] & 0x3f)`.

diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/guid.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/guid.rs
